{"id": "EUVD-2026-59238", "enisaUuid": "cfe45d6a-40bd-33a3-b67f-d3b1028eef3a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nqede: fix off-by-one in BD ring consumption on build_skb failure\n\nqede_rx_build_skb() and qede_tpa_rx_build_skb() do not check for a\nNULL return from qede_build_skb(). When it returns NULL under memory\npressure, the functions still consume a BD from the ring before\nreturning NULL. The callers then recycle additional BDs, resulting in\none extra BD being consumed (off-by-one). This desynchronizes the BD\nring, which can corrupt DMA page reference counts and lead to SLUB\nfreelist corruption.\n\nCommit 4e910dbe3650 (\"qede: confirm skb is allocated before using\")\nadded a NULL check inside qede_build_skb() to prevent a NULL pointer\ndereference, but did not address the missing NULL checks in the\ncallers, making this off-by-one reachable.\n\nFix this by adding NULL checks for the return value of\nqede_build_skb() in both qede_rx_build_skb() and\nqede_tpa_rx_build_skb(), returning NULL immediately before any BD ring\nmanipulation.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:55:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:18", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ecc05d4b20220a09c9c69584fc46ca55248a374a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/07be8b8adf91b7ada4c3dacce064d572a6066421", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1624aa100c0b218181aa74e3696a389b509298cb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0bf78df2d3ecb1f4964ff42a7327d25845955153", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/814a5edac8c9fc04051808d5faaa93768e989281", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b066420e57f3402a52c998678b4678252ac9bb63", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/982d6d6bc059c5dff37a2201c2f08c14bcfcbd20", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a0a558ca7e75b49e71f8c545c30e8c005e6e4e2f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-447g-7f2j-g4vp", "CVE-2026-72339"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.75, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1b6337d7-e6ea-3591-a16e-d7df4356544e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a8633978b842c88fbcfe00d4e5dde96048f630e <814a5edac8c9fc04051808d5faaa93768e989281"}, {"id": "25d6b966-2095-3e79-9cdd-880843181273", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.178"}, {"id": "3670490c-f884-376a-83c7-e3965841a80f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a8633978b842c88fbcfe00d4e5dde96048f630e <0bf78df2d3ecb1f4964ff42a7327d25845955153"}, {"id": "380d54e5-99fd-31f5-9338-6d01d1a2eba9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "482dea3c-1c33-3aa8-9c23-3130b7298777", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a8633978b842c88fbcfe00d4e5dde96048f630e <a0a558ca7e75b49e71f8c545c30e8c005e6e4e2f"}, {"id": "4ea15783-58e6-3e55-8f7d-a474d3f4eccf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a8633978b842c88fbcfe00d4e5dde96048f630e <07be8b8adf91b7ada4c3dacce064d572a6066421"}, {"id": "4f579535-d5c4-37a2-8583-6ceaa66f0f88", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.261"}, {"id": "6397da97-e755-3497-911f-8bcd2b5e391e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a8633978b842c88fbcfe00d4e5dde96048f630e <ecc05d4b20220a09c9c69584fc46ca55248a374a"}, {"id": "6d92f632-9a7d-3cb5-af11-cd9bbe2f9798", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.212"}, {"id": "793efd0b-f836-3f00-a8a6-4a38eb546cd4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8a8633978b842c88fbcfe00d4e5dde96048f630e <1624aa100c0b218181aa74e3696a389b509298cb"}, {"id": "964a2194-e6c5-38b5-8d8f-3f6e3120cf14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "produ